        "name": "USN-7930-2",
        "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel. An attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system. This update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:   - Cryptographic API;   - ACPI drivers;   - Hardware monitoring drivers;   - InfiniBand drivers;   - MTD block device drivers;   - Network drivers;   - DesignWare USB3 driver;   - Ceph distributed file system;   - Network file system (NFS) server daemon;   - NILFS2 file system;   - File systems infrastructure;   - Tracing infrastructure;   - Appletalk network protocol;   - IPv6 networking;   - Netfilter; (CVE-2021-47146, CVE-2021-47269, CVE-2021-47385, CVE-2021-47634, CVE-2022-49026, CVE-2024-49935, CVE-2024-50067, CVE-2024-50095, CVE-2024-50179, CVE-2024-53112, CVE-2024-53217, CVE-2025-21715, CVE-2025-21722, CVE-2025-21811, CVE-2025-21855, CVE-2025-38666, CVE-2025-39964, CVE-2025-40018)",
